# Cache

This app ships with a cache manager backed by `github.com/goforj/cache`.

The generated setup uses:

- one default cache
- many named caches
- the same API regardless of backend

## Defaults

By default, the scaffold defines:

- the default cache from `CACHE_*`
- additional named caches from `CACHE_<NAME>_*`

## Configuration

Use these environment variables:

```env
CACHE_DRIVER=memory
CACHE_DEFAULT_TTL_SECONDS=300
CACHE_PREFIX=app

CACHE_SESSIONS_DRIVER=file
CACHE_SESSIONS_FILE_DIR=.cache/sessions

CACHE_RATE_LIMITS_DRIVER=sqlite
CACHE_RATE_LIMITS_DSN=.cache/rate-limits.db
CACHE_RATE_LIMITS_PREFIX=rate-limits
```

Supported drivers in the scaffold resolver:

- `memory`
- `file`
- `memcached`
- `dynamodb`
- `sqlite`
- `postgres`
- `mysql`
- `nats`
- `redis`
- `null`

Common env vars:

| Env var suffix | Value type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| DRIVER | string | memory |
| DEFAULT_TTL_SECONDS | integer seconds | 300 |
| PREFIX | string | app |
| COMPRESSION | string | none |
| MAX_VALUE_BYTES | integer bytes | 0 |
| ENCRYPTION_KEY | string | empty |

Driver-specific env vars:

| Driver | Env var suffix | Value type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| memory | MEMORY_CLEANUP_SECONDS | integer seconds | 600 |
| file | FILE_DIR | path | temp directory under the OS temp root |
| memcached | ADDRESSES | comma-separated host:port list | empty |
| dynamodb | ENDPOINT | URL | empty |
| dynamodb | REGION | string | us-east-1 |
| dynamodb | TABLE | string | cache_entries |
| sqlite | DSN | string | temp sqlite file for the cache name |
| sqlite | TABLE | string | cache_entries |
| postgres | DSN | string | empty |
| postgres | TABLE | string | cache_entries |
| mysql | DSN | string | empty |
| mysql | TABLE | string | cache_entries |
| nats | URL | URL | NATS_URL or nats://127.0.0.1:4222 |
| nats | BUCKET | string | derived from the cache name |
| nats | BUCKET_TTL | duration string | empty |
| nats | BUCKET_TTL_SECONDS | integer seconds | 0 |
| nats | DESCRIPTION | string | empty |
| nats | HISTORY | integer | 1 |
| nats | MAX_BYTES | integer bytes | 0 |
| nats | MAX_VALUE_SIZE | integer bytes | 0 |
| nats | REPLICAS | integer | 1 |
| nats | STORAGE | string | file |
| nats | COMPRESSED | boolean | false |
| redis | ADDR | host:port | REDIS_HOST:REDIS_PORT or redis:6379 |
| redis | USERNAME | string | empty |
| redis | PASSWORD | string | REDIS_PASSWORD or empty |
| redis | DB | integer | REDIS_DB or 0 |
| redis | TLS | boolean | false |
| redis | INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY | boolean | false |
| null | none | n/a | no driver-specific env vars |

## Driver Optimization

Cache drivers are added to the generated app on demand.

When you run:

```bash
forj generate --cache
```

GoForj inspects:

- `CACHE_*` for the default cache
- `CACHE_<NAME>_*` for named caches

Then it generates cache config code that imports only the optional drivers your app is actually using.

Examples:

- memory-only apps pull only the root `github.com/goforj/cache` module
- memory + file apps still use only the root cache module
- apps that add Memcached pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/memcachedcache` only when needed
- apps that add DynamoDB pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/dynamocache` only when needed
- apps that add SQLite pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/sqlitecache` only when needed
- apps that add Postgres pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/postgrescache` only when needed
- apps that add MySQL pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/mysqlcache` only when needed
- apps that add NATS pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/natscache` only when needed
- apps that add Redis pull `github.com/goforj/cache/driver/rediscache` only when needed

`forj build` also runs cache generation automatically before building the app binary.

## Usage

```go
err := app.Cache().SetString("health", "ok", 0)
```

Resolve a named cache:

```go
sessions := app.Caches().Sessions()
limits := app.Caches().RateLimits()
```

## Notes

- File cache paths default to a temp dir when `FILE_DIR` is not set.
- Named file caches default to isolated subdirectories under the temp cache root.
- Run `forj generate --cache` after adding or renaming named caches when you want to refresh cache code directly.
- `forj generate` also regenerates cache accessors and optional cache driver imports.
- `forj build` runs the same cache generation step automatically before building.
